From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Well: background apps stay in view; one app per status item

The Well showed only kept apps; every other status item went behind a
generic grid button, even when it was the only one, so the overflow
revealed a single app at the cost of the same room. It now shows status
items while they fit (four on a desktop or tablet, fewer on a narrower
screen) and folds the rest only when two or more would be hidden. The
overflow shows the stacked faces of the apps it holds and their count.

A Chromium-family browser names every status icon chrome_status_icon_<n>
and draws in it whichever app asked, so a web app's icon was named after
the browser ("Chrome"). A status item now resolves to one installed app:
its own desktop entry; for a browser's item, the web app its tooltip names
(desktop entry <browser>-<id>-<profile>.desktop or StartupWMClass crx_<id>),
else the browser. Name, face and the key a pin keeps all come from that
app. A browser's notification whose origin is an installed web app's site
is placed under the web app. The rules live in lumaWellModel.js, without
gi imports, so %check runs them.

